description: Limit real-vehicle changes and say which checks were not run.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Vehicle and verification

- Do not flash firmware, arm, disarm, erase on-board logs, reboot, or write parameters unless the user explicitly asks for that action.
- Do not turn safe mode on while checking the UI. Opening the checklist and closing it is allowed.
- A compile, unit test, or open page is not a live vehicle check. Say which of the UI, the bridge, and the vehicle link were not exercised.
- Use mock or SITL when a change itself must be sent. Testing does not replace the user's confirmation.
